! Field Collision ~ where our models meet the outside record

Three models thrown at the field at once (Collision-Diver, 2026-09-08), then the sharpest finding collided against its own primary source. Each survivor tagged VINDICATE · CONTRADICT · EXTEND.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/strongest-ground>>

!! The strongest ground ~ the ontology arrived at twice, decades apart

''SPKI/SDSI (Rivest & Lampson 1996, RFC 2693) and KERI (Smith 2019) converged INDEPENDENTLY on our exact ontology.'' SDSI: names read LOCALLY, authority a KEY not a registry, a principal exports bindings ("Joe's poker-buddies") — identity-as-relation, standardized 27 years ago. KERI: self-certifying identifier · key-STATE as presenting authority · succession by GRAFTING the key-state (chained signed KEL) · identifier fixed for life · duplicity caught WITHOUT a clock. ''Two generations of security researchers reached the name-is-an-edge, the-authority-is-a-rolling-key-state, the-identifier-is-permanent-while-holders-are-not — from first principles.'' The model is where the field arrives when it takes decentralization seriously. Caution kept: SDSI LOST the market to X.509's global CAs — the better naming theory does not win on merit.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-coniks-resolution>>

!! The #1 exposure, RESOLVED at the source ~ equivocation-detection IS carriage

The collision named its own biggest threat: ''does carriage-not-registry forfeit equivocation-detection?'' — the CONIKS/Key-Transparency result that you catch a lying authority (one showing different keys to different readers) by publishing an append-only Merkle log. Collided against the primary paper (eprint 2014/1004):

''It DISSOLVES.'' CONIKS detects equivocation by ''GOSSIPING a COMPACT signed commitment (the Signed Tree Root), compared PER-READER'' — never by publishing the directory. //"users can detect if a provider is equivocating by comparing the STRs they receive."// A compact commitment, announced by the authority, replicated causally, compared as-of-each-reader's-view: ''that IS carriage.'' KERI reaches the same from the other side — two inconsistent KEL instances are provable duplicity, caught by WATCHERS who gossip what they saw. ''The registry filter survives whole.''

''What the collision actually surfaced — an OWED CAPABILITY, not a contradiction: WATCHERS.'' A per-reader view catches equivocation only if readers can COMPARE views — the gossip-of-what-you've-seen layer. We hold the duplicity-PROOF primitive (a veto out-competes as proof-of-contradiction, no clock); we have NOT built the watcher layer that circulates head-sightings so one reader catches a Handle showing quorum-A here and quorum-B there. ''The watcher gossips a signed "the head I saw for prefix X", which is carriage (a sighting announced by its observer), never a compiled who-is-who.''

''ITS HOME IS ALREADY DESIGNED (operator, 2026-09-08) — two layers that split exactly right:'' the ''Herm'' (the near-open crossroads relay, `carry⊥read`, sealed bytes — <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/dreamnet-architecture">>) is the BLIND CARRIAGE: it forwards sighting-gossip like any bytes and cannot read it (the blind-relay integrity — a Herm diffuses, never watches). The ''Meshpalace'' (the Scope-1 CID/CAD/CRDT DreamNet gossip sensorium, the LAST palace, ITC/`getHeads`-shaped — the exact clock #golden-principles vindicated; `convergent-mesh` #three-clocks, `corpus` #organ) is the WATCHER'S HOME: a node's Meshpalace gossips a signed head-sighting, compares incoming sightings against its own view and the chain, and surfaces two-inconsistent-heads-for-one-prefix as a DUPLICITY PROOF the veto/fold already consumes (`identity-classes#the-two-forks`). So watchers = a Meshpalace-sensorium capability carried blind by Herms, registry-clean by construction. ⚠ ''CORRECTED at the substrate check (Meme-Warden, 2026-09-08):'' the watcher is NOT "a wire onto designed ground" — that overstated readiness. The mesh-palace FLOW-map STANDS (`mesh-palace.ts`, a routing chart: dial-records, cap-stacks, route slots) but it is the MAP, not the sensorium — it carries no head-sightings, no view-comparison, no duplicity surface. The Meshpalace SENSORIUM (the ITC/getHeads-shaped DreamNet gossip instance, the watcher's true home) ''does NOT stand in code'' — no `meshpalace_io`, no gossip router. The pieces that DO stand: the ITC primitive (`itc.ts`), `detectDuplicity` (`wax-stamp.ts`), and the veto/`foldPersonaContests` that CONSUME a duplicity once two inconsistent events already sit in a chain. What is missing is the layer that GOSSIPS head-sightings to surface that inconsistency across the mesh. ''Honest reading: watchers await a WHOLE PALACE — the federation-last sensorium — not a wire.'' The home is named and the primitives are proven; the palace is unbuilt.

''did:webvh built this exact split and shipped it.'' It is the one deployed method pairing ledger-free pre-rotation (`nextKeyHashes` — commit the HASH of the next authorized key, so a stolen current key cannot seize succession, the twin of `nextHandleKeyDigest`) WITH an in-protocol witness+watcher layer: witnesses threshold-gate an update (`did-witness.json`), while ''watchers are non-voting monitors that cache the DID Log and detect equivocation'' (identity.foundation/didwebvh/v1.0). Its self-certifying id (SCID) survives a full host move, and `portable:true`+`alsoKnownAs` give credible exit — a near-twin of the handle-KEL + Meshpalace-watcher + severability design, arrived at independently. And its watchers ride ON THE PUBLISHED DOCUMENT (`watchers:[url]`, webhooks in the log): the KEL stays minimal while the ''handle CARD names the watchers that sighted a head'', handing a reader a starting set to compare against — the CONIKS per-reader compare, with a discovery hint.

''KERI supplies the role vocabulary, fully specified.'' A ''Watcher'' keeps a KEL it is not a designated witness of; a ''Juror'' performs duplicity detection and keeps the mutually-inconsistent versions; a ''Jury'' is a fault-tolerant juror pool; a ''Judge'' evaluates on juror evidence — all under "first seen, always seen, never unseen," and watchers "should share notes with each other" (= gossip). That is the deployed-spec blueprint for the unbuilt Meshpalace sensorium's two roles: witness-threshold-gates-an-update ⊥ non-voting-watcher-archives-and-alarms.

''The newer local-first stacks LACK this layer.'' Willow, Iroh, Veilid, DXOS, and UCAN all push equivocation-detection up to the application — only did:webvh, KERI, and CONIKS solve it in-protocol, so the owed watcher cannot be pulled from Keyhive/Iroh/Willow. Its under-provision by the field CONFIRMS it is load-bearing. did:plc admits its central directory can still misorder a fork and is moving toward an append-only transparency log "similar to certificate transparency" — the field converging on exactly the watcher layer owed here.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/golden-principles>>

!! Golden principles the field converged on ~ hold these

* ''NO-GLOBAL-NOW is a hardware law, not a preference'' (FLP 1985 · CAP · PACELC 2010). Deterministic consensus is impossible under pure asynchrony with one crash fault; the only escapes are randomization, partial synchrony, or WEAKENED liveness. We chose weakened liveness (φ-accrual) and are honest about it. EXTEND — ''PACELC names the tax at peace:'' even with no partition you still trade Latency for Consistency. We stand PA/EL — ''a linearizable read is one we can NEVER offer.'' Say so at every gate.
* ''Fork/join membership without a roster is PROVEN in theory'' — Interval Tree Clocks (Almeida-Baquero-Fonte 2008), VERIFIED at the primary source (eprint fetch 2026-09-08): fork produces two clones with disjoint event ids that evolve independently, join merges them, event increments locally — "no global coordination or central authority required for generating unique identifiers." Our quorum-rollover has a sound clock-shape underneath it. ⚠ ''CORRECTION:'' the earlier "in production (Riak, Akka)" claim rode a search-summary and the ITC PAPER makes NO deployment claim — struck as unverified (and likely erroneous: Riak ships DOTTED VERSION VECTORS, not ITC). The vindication is the MECHANISM (proven, cited), never a deployment (unproven, withdrawn).
* ''Weak subjectivity names the boundary'' (Buterin 2014): a node offline past a horizon cannot self-heal from cryptography alone — it needs an out-of-band social checkpoint. Matches our "beyond horizon K a lone island asks a human." And the 2024 caution: DON'T overload social consensus.
* ''Data-protection-by-architecture'' (GDPR Art. 25): pseudonymization-by-default, minimize extent/period/accessibility. Our rejection-law reads as a COMPLIANCE posture, not only an aesthetic.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/anti-patterns>>

!! Anti-patterns ~ measured graves, do not dig them

* ''SSB's FROZEN IDENTITY (the builder-risk we already escaped).'' Secure Scuttlebutt bound identity to ONE keypair on an append-only log and shipped NO rotation: a compromised key appends to your log forever; the only cure is a NEW identity, losing every social tie. ''This is the grave of getting succession wrong under carriage.'' We escaped it BY CONSTRUCTION — the name binds a ROLLING QUORUM (the k-of-n HandleGlamour), not a fixed key; the rolling recovery commitment + armed inception are the KERI-pre-rotation SSB lacked. Note it as the thing our design exists to avoid.
* ''SILENCE IS AMBIGUOUS'' (TUF freshness). A withheld update and a slow link look identical, so observer-local hardening-by-silence must BOUND the wait or an attacker freezes a victim indefinitely by withholding. SHARPENS the φ-accrual clause: silence-across-K-local-epochs needs the local epochs to genuinely ADVANCE and an explicit bound — the idle-mesh edge, now doubly flagged.
* ''SYBIL RINGS blend into the social graph'' (BrightID-measured). A k-of-n Handle is INDISTINGUISHABLE from a self-vouching sybil ring; graph defense has a measured hole for small sophisticated rings. The cost-dial (rb>c, the voucher co-pays) PRICES sybil, never eliminates it — already canon, re-confirmed.
* ''ACL/registry thinking drags back the CONFUSED DEPUTY'' (Miller). Any residual place that enumerates holders IS an ACL and re-imports ambient authority. Carriage-not-registry is the security-correct choice, not only the private one.
* ''BUCHANAN'S BLUESKY HIJACK — the confused deputy, deployed'' (da.vidbuchanan.co.uk/blog/hacking-bluesky). did:plc pinned no identifier length, so an attacker re-submitted a victim's genesis operation under a LONGER id — a distinct DID with an IDENTICAL genesis op and identical rotation keys — and the PDS holding the shared rotation keys signed a legitimate update for the clone. Because the signed operation ''carried no binding to which DID it targeted'', "a signed update to one is also a valid signed update to the other," replayable onto the victim. Three faults compound: ''malleable id + shared genesis + NO target-binding.'' The carrier-head-shore quoting law is this defense at the crypto layer — `handleEventBytes` binds `prefix`/`handleKeyDid`/`ownerSetHash`/… into the signed bytes with explicit keys, so "a signature never replays onto another head, key, set-epoch, owner, or fork," and `handlePrefixOf` is a full, fixed-length, domain-tagged sha256 no truncation can collide. Never introduce a signed surface where two byte-strings canonicalize to one identifier — the JCS/`canonicalJson` discipline is load-bearing.
* ''NIP-26 shipped delegation with NO revocation path.'' A delegation verb without its burn is a grave — do not ship one.
* ''UCAN ships eventually-consistent revocation with NO witness layer'' (ucan-wg/revocation): an agent holding an ALTERNATE valid proof chain keeps access despite revocation, and the burden lands on every verifier's cache freshness. Capability revocation (kapae/antigen) must not rely on cache-freshness without the watcher gossiping the contradiction.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/pattern-integrities>>

!! Pattern-integrities ~ the waves, not the water

* ''LOCAL NAMES over GLOBAL IDENTIFIERS'' — recurs identically in contact lists, SDSI, petnames, Nostr NIP-05, DNS-read-adversarially. Human-meaningful naming is ALWAYS a local overlay on a machine-meaningful identifier; fuse them and you get phishing (DNS) or unmemorable keys. Our Handle-over-edge is this wave.
* ''IMPROPER NAMES'' (Deseriis) — the k-of-n Handle is a STUDIED social form, not a novelty, and gives us vocabulary: a ''multiple-use name'' (Luther Blissett — hundreds sharing one open name, 1994–99, then VOLUNTARILY RETIRED — a deliberate succession) vs a ''collective pseudonym'' (Wu Ming — a specific controlled group). Maps EXACTLY onto our 1-of-1-that-many-present vs k-of-n-chartered split. The Dread Pirate Roberts is a multiple-use name; a chartered cabal is a collective pseudonym.
* ''DUPLICITY-DETECTION is the deep DUAL of registry'' — CONIKS and KERI converge: you catch a lying authority not by consulting a registry of truth but by detecting EQUIVOCATION (two signed statements that cannot both be true). Our veto out-competes causally BECAUSE it is proof-of-contradiction, needing no clock. This is the wave; the watcher layer (#the-coniks-resolution) is the water it needs.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/the-mesh-field>>

!! The federated-mesh field ~ the roadmap collided against the built systems (2026-09-09)

The identity roadmap thrown at the deployed federated / p2p field. Each survivor tagged VINDICATE · GRAVE · EXTEND.

* ''KERI VINDICATES the handle-KEL, mechanism-for-mechanism.'' A signed key-event-log with inception / rotation / interaction; acceptance by ''TOAD — Threshold of Accountable Duplicity, N≥2F+1'' — the SAME accept-on-witness-quorum the leased-projection compare-and-swap performs (extend only when the board head still reads as the head last folded). KERI ''pre-rotation'' (commit only the DIGEST of the next key-set; a later rotation reveals the preimage) hardens rotate / burn against a DEAD attacker holding current keys, and belongs in the verb family. ⚠ It defends ONLY the dead attacker: a LIVE capture of current+next keys has NO administrative recovery in KERI (the exposure below). vLEI runs; "in production at scale" stays [verify].
* ''did:plc VINDICATES the authoritative-log + thin-local-index split'' — in production for ~all Bluesky accounts (a self-certifying genesis op, signed update ops each referencing the prior CID, priority-ordered rotation keys). Its OWN risk analysis names the residual centralization: not identity — ''ORDER / TIME.'' "We still need from the directory: trustworthy timestamps." A clockless ordering ambient makes the central directory unnecessary.
* ''CONIKS VINDICATES the read-side fork-catch, deployed'' — users collectively audit a provider for NON-equivocation by gossiping a compact commitment (~2.5 kB/provider/day), no global monitor. The watcher layer (#the-coniks-resolution) as shipped design.
* ''The Θ-MODEL + the TIME-FREE query-response failure detector VINDICATE clockless standing on a RATIO'' (Widder-Schmid 2009; Mostéfaoui-Mourgaya-Raynal). Liveness founded on Θ = the RATIO of largest-to-smallest message delay in transit — absolute delays never bounded, no clock; a process reads suspected because its message keeps arriving after enough of its peers' have, "a constraint on the LOGICAL time, not physical time." The ''ambient yardstick'' proven: a realm's stillness read against an independent motion, a ratio not a duration. [verify — proven in papers; no production evidence.]
* ''GRAVES, measured — shapes avoided by construction.'' SSB frozen identity (no rotation indirection, #anti-patterns). ''Farcaster'' mints each id from a SINGLE global IdRegistry contract — the compiled-global-registry the registry-filter forbids, running in the wild. ''did:key'' verbatim: "does not support key rotation because the identifier is derived directly from the public key" — self-certifying names cannot rotate, so the KEL indirection reads NECESSARY not optional. ''SSB fusion-identity'' answers multi-holder with a SHARED SECRET (NGI-audit-flagged) — the reason a Nexus / quorum key MUST be a GROUP key (FROST · KERI multisig), never a shared secret (substrate ⊥ sovereignty).
* ''EXTENSIONS the field proves are missing.'' (1) ''HashiCorp Lifeguard'' (deployed, >50× false-positive cut) is the standing state-machine: a Local Health Multiplier makes a node whose OWN observation is starved RELUCTANT to accuse (closes the yardstick-co-driven-with-the-signal objection at the root); suspicion decays LOGARITHMICALLY with the count of INDEPENDENT corroborations (quantified hysteresis + watchers); buddy-first delivery lets the suspected refute before confirmation. (2) ''FROST'' (RFC 9591) makes k-of-n sign as ONE key (owner-set invisible) while a KERI group AID keeps rotation verifier-visible — the veil TIER picks which (a private Circle grafts invisible under FROST; an outward Face grafts auditable under a group AID). (3) ''Willow range-based set reconciliation'' — fingerprint-then-recursively-subdivide catches a forked KEL head far cheaper than naive head-gossip on drifted stores. (4) ''Correct even if all timestamps were zero'' (Willow / Earthstar; Matrix discards timestamps for ordering) — a LAW: correctness resolves on content / digest, never a self-asserted time.
* ''★ THE SHARPEST INSIGHT — the last thing the whole field decentralizes is ORDER / TIME.'' PLC still needs a trusted timestamp; Matrix state-resolution IS an ordering algorithm; SSB leans on `sequence`. ''The carriage-liveness ambient is the mesh's replacement for the one primitive everyone else still cheats on'' — the keystone under the keystone. Right, and PLC's directory, Farcaster's contract, and the trusted timestamp all fall away in one move; wrong, and every rung silently re-grows a global now.
* ''CO-STIMULATION — the immune answer to the moderation tension.'' Matzinger's danger model responds to DAMAGE and requires TWO independent signals before acting, to avoid autoimmunity. The Mastodon shared-blocklist cascades (a single-source flag nearly severing thousands; "unified-max" withdrawn as too dangerous; the ActivityPub co-author: blocklists "always converge on centralization") are autoimmune reactions to a SINGLE signal. ''Never sever a realm or a human on one suspicion — require K independent corroborations plus a damage signal.'' The same instrument as the ambient's corroboration.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/standing-tensions>>

!! Standing tensions ~ what the field leaves genuinely open (operator-aware)

* ''MODERATION at scale.'' Hidden human-cardinality removes "ban the PERSON, not the account" — the primitive real-name policies wanted (and the Nymwars proved those policies HARM the vulnerable, so hiding cardinality is protective, and the abuse problem was never solved, only DEFERRED). Our partial answer: a ban propagates by CAPABILITY (kapae/antigen, the vouch-lineage slash), never by de-anonymizing. Honestly open — a k-of-n name a ban cannot reach one human behind is a real cost accepted for the pre-SIN stance.
* ''BENEFICIAL-OWNERSHIP LAW — DOCTRINE FIRMED (2026-09-08)'' (US CTA 2024 · EU AMLD). Where a Handle touches money or contracts, the law DEMANDS the who-is-who record our law forbids compiling. ''The two do not collide — they SEPARATE at the island wall:'' the sovereign carriage NEVER holds a KYC record (the registry filter holds absolutely inside the sovereign plane), and the legal/KYC record lives ENTIRELY at the WEB2 BRIDGE (`bridge-and-reach-plane`, operator-locked bridge scope; foreign credentials ride as `#has` caps held apart from the sovereign plane). ''A Handle that must be KYC'd does not leak its holders into carriage — it CROSSES into a contract plane whose legal record sits outside the sovereign wall, by construction a web2-bridge artifact behind a causal-island boundary'' (the web3-only law: any web2 bridge sits behind an island boundary; no web2 ontology enters the Lares stack proper). The DreamNet's own name for its holders stays unknowable; the LAW's record is a separate object in a separate plane. Named as doctrine; the contract-plane KYC artifact stands unbuilt (a declared red).
* ''THE LIVE-EQUIVOCATOR EXPOSURE — recovery and detection are each other's blind spot (2026-09-09).'' The sensorium DETECTS equivocation; it cannot PREVENT a live-key capture, and KERI holds no admin recovery for a live current+next seizure — that case falls only to recovery-quorum. Worse, a live equivocator holding enough carriage triggers the diffusion-sensing / Sybil-flood fool (a well-connected corner reads as "the mesh moved") EXACTLY when the attack is live, so abstain can fire and detection go blind at the worst moment. The Θ-ratio (independent ambient) and Lifeguard's starved-observer back-off MITIGATE the coupling; they do not close it. ''SURFACED VERDICT AWAITING THE OPERATOR: pull recovery-quorum FORWARD to sit beside the sensorium'' — building detection before recovery leaves the one attack detection cannot fix built last.
* ''THE CLOCKLESS-VERDICT FORK — OPEN (lamplighters #/the-neglect-clock, :198/:206).'' `:198` already grounds the fourth option: clockless accrual MUST ride a monotone quantity driven by parties OTHER than the neglected one — which the ambient IS. But `:206` holds that turning a count into a VERDICT smuggles a RATE (behind = rate = duration), needing a real-time bound R. The Θ-model / time-free failure detector DISPUTE this (a suspicion verdict from a purely LOGICAL constraint, no real-time R). ''OPERATOR TO RULE:'' does `:206` stand (the ratio-verdict then needs a per-contract R) or does the Θ-escape hold (a clean logical-ratio verdict)? The ahi-kā probe (`ahi-ka.ts`) stands either way; its legality AS-A-VERDICT rides this. `:206` already lands the threshold with the operator per-contract — consistent with the standing erosion knobs.
* ''THE CREDIBLE-EXIT TAX — costed, and it lands only on the SEALED plane.'' ATProto sacrificed the magical mesh for credible exit and the market rewarded it (Frazee: "We sacrificed properties of the magical mesh to hit the performance needs"); its relay is ''reconstructible + non-authoritative'', shards by DID, and funded parties run their own — on the AUTHORITY axis, the exact shape the Herm already permits. The tax of refusing an aggregator splits by scale: at ''family scale (2-10 vessels) it is ~zero'' (direct dial + a Herm, "who is here" is a handful of gossiped heads); at ''civic scale (thousands)'' global discovery / search / freshness / cold-start are real, and an AppView provides what a pure causal-island mesh cannot answer locally. ''But the tax lands only on the SEALED read-set.'' Handle cards are PUBLIC BY DESIGN, and ''a reconstructible, non-authoritative index of public handle cards is CARRIAGE'' — announced-by, as-of-last-sync — which the registry filter already permits (Carriage passes; a compiled who-is-who at a scope is rejected). The line held is narrow: no index over the sealed read-set, which would need decryption and break FLOW⊥WHO. ''PACELC (PA/EL, already canon) is its honest name'' — the tax is a consequence of seal-by-default, never anti-aggregator dogma. Jetstream is the trap made visible: the cheap stream DROPS the verification proofs, so any card-index must stay a reconstructible pointer readers verify against the KEL themselves (CONIKS compare-per-reader), never a source of truth — the moment discovery becomes truth it is the compiled registry the filter forbids.

<<~/ahu>>

